  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a photograph of the World Trade Center towers in New York City, overlaid with text that reads 'we said we would never forget' at the top and 'why are you voting them into our government?' at the bottom. The visual material (the towers) is juxtaposed with the textual material to evoke the 9/11 terrorist attacks and to express outrage or condemnation toward political figures or parties perceived as being associated with those attacks. The intent is to provoke emotional response and to question the electorate's choice to support such figures, potentially leading to harmful consequences such as increased polarization, division, or even violence. The meme does not contain explicit hate speech or discriminatory language targeting specific protected groups, but its message is politically charged and potentially inflammatory, which can contribute to societal harm by inciting anger and distrust. The overall intent is propagandistic, aiming to influence political opinion and action by leveraging the trauma of 9/11 to discredit political opponents or policies.",
